mmit date\nL188: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL189: cite79†docs | cite79†docs |    |\nL190: cite80†figures | cite80†figures |    |\nL191: cite81†LICENSE | cite81†LICENSE |    |\nL192: cite82†README.md | cite82†README.md |    |\nL193: cite83†tech_report.pdf | cite83†tech_report.pdf |    |\nL194: \nL195: ## Repository files navigation\nL196: \nL197:   *   * cite84†README L198:   * cite84†License L199: \nL200: More items\nL201: \nL202: cite85†Image: Kimi K2.5 L203: \nL204: * * *\nL205: \nL206: 📰  cite86†Tech Blog†www.kimi.com |     📄  cite83†Full Report L207: ## 1. Model Introduction\nL208: \nL209: Kimi K2.5 is an open-source, native multimodal agentic model built through continual pretraining on approximately 15 trillion mixed visual and text tokens atop Kimi-K2-Base. It seamlessly integrates vision and language understanding with advanced agentic capabilities, instant and thinking modes, as well as conversational and agentic paradigms.\nL210: ### Key Features\nL211:   * Native Multimodality: Pre-trained on vision–language tokens, K2.5 excels in visual knowledge, cross-modal reasoning, and agentic tool use grounded in visual inputs.\nL212:   * Coding with Vision: K2.5 generates code from visual specifications (UI designs, video workflows) and autonomously orchestrates tools for visual data processing.\nL213:   * Agent Swarm: K2.5 transitions from single-agent scaling to a self-directed, coordinated swarm-like execution scheme. It decomposes complex tasks into parallel sub-tasks executed by dynamically instantiated, domain-specific agents.\nL214: ## 2. Model Summary\nL215:  |\nL216: --- | ---\nL217: Architecture  | Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)\nL218: Total Parameters  | 1T\nL219: Activated Parameters  | 32B\nL220: Number of Layers (Dense layer included)  | 61\nL221: Number of Dense Layers  | 1\nL222: Attention Hidden Dimension  | 7168\nL223: MoE Hidden Dimension (per Expert)  | 2048\nL224: Number of Attention Heads  | 64\nL225: Number of Experts  | 384\nL226: Selected Experts per Token  | 8\nL227: Number of Shared Experts  | 1\nL228: Vocabulary Size  | 160K\nL229: Context Length  | 256K\nL230: Attention Mechanism  | MLA\nL231: Activation Function  | SwiGLU\nL232: Vision Encoder  | MoonViT\nL233: Parameters of Vision Encoder  | 400M\nL234: ## 3. Evaluation Results\nL235: Benchmark  | ^{Kimi K2.5\nL236: ^{(Thinking)}}  | ^{GPT-5.2\nL237: ^{(xhigh)}}  | ^{Claude 4.5 Opus\nL238: ^{(Extended Thinking)}}  | ^{Gemini 3 Pro\nL239: ^{(High Thinking Level)}}  | ^{DeepSeek V3.2\nL240: ^{(Thinking)}}  | ^{Qwen3-VL-\nL241: 235B-A22B-\nL242: Thinking}\nL243: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL244: Reasoning & Knowledge\nL245: HLE-Full  | 30.1  | 34.5  | 30.8  | 37.5  | 25.1^{†}  | -\nL246: HLE-Full\nL247: (w/ tools)  | 50.2  | 45.5  | 43.2  | 45.8  | 40.8^{†}  | -\nL248: AIME 2025  | 96.1  | 100  | 92.8  | 95.0  | 93.1  | -\nL249: HMMT 2025 (Feb)  | 95.4  | 99.4  | 92.9*  | 97.3*  | 92.5  | -\nL250: IMO-AnswerBench  | 81.8  | 86.3  | 78.5*  | 83.1*  | 78.3  | -\nL251: GPQA-Diamond  | 87.6  | 92.4  | 87.0  | 91.9  | 82.4  | -\nL252: MMLU-Pro  | 87.1  | 86.7*  | 89.3*  | 90.1  | 85.0  | -\nL253: Image & Video\nL254: MMMU-Pro  | 78.5  | 79.5*  | 74.0  | 81.0  | -  | 69.3\nL255: CharXiv (RQ)  | 77.5  | 82.1  | 67.2*  | 81.4  | -  | 66.1\nL256: MathVision  | 84.2  | 83.0  | 77.1*  | 86.1*  | -  | 74.6\nL257: MathVista (mini)  | 90.1  | 82.8*  | 80.2*  | 89.8*  | -  | 85.8\nL258: ZeroBench  | 9  | 9*  | 3*  | 8*  | -  | 4*\nL259: ZeroBench\nL260: (w/ tools)  | 11  | 7*  | 9*  | 12*  | -  | 3*\nL261: OCRBench  | 92.3  | 80.7*  | 86.5*  | 90.3*  | -  | 87.5\nL262: OmniDocBench 1.5  | 88.8  | 85.7  | 87.7*  | 88.5  | -  | 82.0*\nL263: InfoVQA (val)  | 92.6  | 84*  | 76.9*  | 57.2*  | -  | 89.5\nL264: SimpleVQA  | 71.2  | 55.8*  | 69.7*  | 69.7*  | -  | 56.8*\nL265: cite87†WorldVQA | 46.3  | 28.0  | 36.8  | 47.4  | -  | 23.5\nL266: VideoMMMU  | 86.6  | 85.9  | 84.4*  | 87.6  | -  | 80.0\nL267: MMVU  | 80.4  |