301:      * Unless otherwise specified, all Kimi K2.5 experiments were conducted with temperature = 1.0, top-p = 0.95, and a context length of 256k tokens.\nL302:      * Benchmarks without publicly available scores were re-evaluated under the same conditions used for Kimi K2.5 and are marked with an asterisk (*).\nL303:      * We could not evaluate GPT-5.2 xhigh on all benchmarks due to service stability issues. For benchmarks that were not tested, we mark them as \"-\".\nL304:   2. Text and Reasoning\nL305:      * HLE, AIME 2025, HMMT 2025 (Feb), and GPQA-Diamond were evaluated with a maximum completion budget of 96k tokens.\nL306:      * Results for AIME and HMMT are averaged over 32 runs (avg@32); GPQA-Diamond over 8 runs (avg@8).\nL307:      * For HLE, we report scores on the full set (text & image). Kimi K2.5 scores 31.5 (text) and 21.3 (image) without tools, and 51.8 (text) and 39.8 (image) with tools. The DeepSeek-V3.2 score corresponds to its text-only subset (marked with †) . Hugging Face access was blocked to prevent potential data leakage. HLE with tools uses simple context management: once the context exceeds a threshold, only the latest round of tool messages is retained.\nL308:   3. Tool-Augmented / Agentic Search\nL309:      * Kimi K2.5 was equipped with search, code-interpreter, and web-browsing tools for HLE with tools and all agentic search benchmarks.\nL310:      * Except for BrowseComp (where K2.5 and DeepSeek-V3.2 used the discard-all strategy), no context management was applied, and tasks exceeding the supported context length were directly counted as failed.\nL311:      * The test system prompts emphasize deep and proactive tool use, instructing models to reason carefully, leverage tools, and verify uncertain information. Full prompts will be provided in the technical report.\nL312:      * Results for Seal-0 and WideSearch are averaged over four runs (avg@4).\nL313:   4. Vision Benchmarks\nL314:      * Max-tokens = 64k, averaged over three runs (avg@3).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - Tencent/llm.hunyuan.T1 · GitHub (https://github.com/Tencent/llm.hunyuan.T1)\nciteturn31838view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/Tencent/llm.hunyuan.T1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 259\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - QwenLM/Qwen3.8: Qwen3.8 is the large language model series developed by Qwen team, Alibaba Group. · GitHub (https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3.5)\nciteturn31838view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3.5\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3.8; Total lines: 413\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSeed News - ByteDance Seed Team (https://seed.bytedance.com/en/blog/seed2-0-%E6%AD%A3%E5%BC%8F%E5%8F%91%E5%B8%83)\nciteturn31838view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://seed.bytedance.com/en/blog/seed2-0-%E6%AD%A3%E5%BC%8F%E5%8F%91%E5%B8%83\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 179\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNews — Google DeepMind (https://deepmind.google/blog/)\nciteturn31838view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 308\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLatest News from Google Research Blog - Google Research (https://research.google/blog/)\nciteturn31838view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://research.google/blog/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 185\n"
